  "far_field_note": "The far field is vertex-for-vertex with the block at its edge and carries the block's own heights inside it, so a 3D scene can draw it past the edge as a ring and leave the block's own terrain to cover the middle. It exists because the city stands on it.",
  "heightmap_note": "heightmap.png is 16-bit grayscale; a browser cannot read its sample values back, which is the only reason hillshade.png and the two .f32 grids exist at all. The 2D viewer never decodes it; the 3D scene reads heightmap.f32 instead."
